<div id="abe-column-block-c26a34bb-1cfd-48ec-8205-e6c43c88a41a" class="abe-column-block" data-block-type="FancyBlockColumn" data-block-id="167658755" style="width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; display: inline-block; font-size: 16px; vertical-align: top;">
  <table width="100%" align="center" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation" style="table-layout: fixed; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-wrap: break-word; text-align: left; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; border-spacing: 0; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt;">
    <tr>
      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-c26a34bb-1cfd-48ec-8205-e6c43c88a41a-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 5px; border: none;">
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Greetings City of Columbus Partner,</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">The City of Columbus is pleased to invite your organization to an in-person training on the Ohio Ethics Law and how it applies to nonprofit and private sector boards operating in the City's orbit, whether through shared board membership or a mission tied to City programs and initiatives.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">This session will be led by <strong>Susan Willeke of the Ohio Ethics Commission</strong> and is designed for board members of organizations that include City officials or employees among their membership, as well as entities created to support City initiatives or programs. The training will cover how the Ohio Ethics Laws interacts with and applies to the private sector, including what board members need to know about conflicts of interest, disclosure obligations, public contracts and related requirements.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Nonprofit boards with City officials or employees have unique ethical obligations which can affect your organization's interactions and business with the City in ways you may not be aware of. Individuals who serve on boards of entities created to support City initiatives or programs may find themselves navigating questions about their relationship to the City, including constraints upon their ability to contract with the City, and what that means for their obligations under Ohio law.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">This training is an opportunity to demystify those requirements and give all board members a clearer picture of the rules that apply when public service and board service intersect, including how Ohio's Ethics Law may shape what your organization can ask of a City official or employee, what transactions or relationships may require closer scrutiny, and what your board can do to navigate those situations effectively.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>All board members and interested individuals are welcome to attend.</strong> We encourage you to share this invitation broadly with your full board and anyone in your organization who may benefit from this information. City officials will also be present to answer questions and join in the conversation.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">We hope to see you there! Please feel free to reach out to Renata Ramsini (<a href="mailto:RJRamsini@columbus.gov" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">RJRamsini@columbus.gov</a>) with any questions.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Date:</strong> Thursday, June 11<sup>th</sup>, 2026</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Time:</strong> 3:00 to 4:30 p.m.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Location:</strong> 1111 E. Broad Street, Continental Room, Lower Level</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Registration is required.</strong> <a href="https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/019e179dca6d796e9e9688084b0f31a9?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">Please register at https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/019e179dca6d796e9e9688084b0f31a9</a> to reserve your spot.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Parking map:</strong> A map with parking locations and entrance door will be sent after registration.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">We hope to see you there! Please feel free to reach out to Renata Ramsini (<a href="mailto:RJRamsini@columbus.gov" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">RJRamsini@columbus.gov</a>) with any questions.</p>
